=========================

PingPimp
--------
Parts of the network engine (yay_net) and the WebUI's Network tab are derived
from PingPimp.

  Project:   PingPimp — https://github.com/fuckyoustan/PingPimp
  Copyright: (c) fuckyoustan
  License:   Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text: LICENSES/PingPimp-Apache-2.0.txt)

What is derived (Apache-2.0 §4(b): these files carry prominent notices that
they were changed):

  * src/net_presets.cpp — the sysctl value sets for the balanced / game /
    download / streaming / social / outdoor profiles (PingPimp's OP_DEFAULT,
    OP_GAME, OP_DOWNLOAD, OP_STREAMING, OP_SOCIAL, OP_OUTDOOR tables).
  * src/net_policy.cpp — app-category heuristics (classify_pkg), the TCP
    congestion-control preference lists, the big-core IRQ-affinity mask rule.
  * src/net_engine.cpp — the set of tunables behind the toggles (IPv6,
    conntrack, IRQ affinity, ksoftirqd priority, Wi-Fi power-save and
    low-latency mode, network-stats, data saver) and their values.
  * yay-webui/src/helpers/dnsProviders.js — the DNS provider catalogue
    (display names and hostnames).
  * The overall feature set and parts of the WebUI's layout/UX (grouped
    Config page, per-app Boost / Isolate pickers with app icons).

Everything else in yay_net is original to this project and not derived from
PingPimp's code: the daemon (event-driven, no polling), KnobStore snapshot /
restore, the per-app iptables-restore chains, the logcat-event reader, the
shared netlink and daemon utilities, and the tests.

Behavioural differences from PingPimp are listed in README.md ("Network
engine → What changed from PingPimp"). The preset values are PingPimp's; they
have not been independently benchmarked here.

Other dependencies
------------------
nlohmann/json (MIT) is fetched at build time; Vue, Vue Router, Pinia, Vite,
